**Input type:** `.snowsql` — no SNZ client-layer constructs present (no
template tags, no `PUT`/`GET`, no stage DML). The `.snowsql` extension is
retained for validator consistency.

---

## 1. Purpose

This script inserts **new** flight-schedule link records from the staging
table `STAGING.ExpFinalyseInserts` into the base table
`BASE.FLT_FOLDER_LINKS`, but only for rows whose inbound and outbound flight-leg
sequence numbers are both resolved (non-NULL) and for which no identical row
already exists in the target. The grain of one output row is one flight-schedule
link (an inbound flight connected to an outbound flight at a link station) with
its 33 attributes. The `NOT EXISTS` anti-join on all 33 columns is an explicit
application-level dedup that prevents duplicate inserts — the Snowflake
equivalent of a Teradata SET-table insert that silently drops full-row
duplicates.

---

## 2. Clause-by-clause walk-through

### INSERT target list (33 columns)

`BASE.FLT_FOLDER_LINKS ( LINK_STATION_CD, IN_ORIGN_STATION_CD, IN_ALN_CD,
IN_FLT_NO, IN_FLT_SFX_CD, IN_DEP_FLTDT, IN_ARR_FLTDT, IN_ARR_FLTTM,
IN_PAX_TML_CD, IN_GROUND_ACY_CD, IN_SERVICE_TYP, IN_FLT_LEG_SEQ_NO,
OUT_DESTATION_STATION_CD, OUT_ALN_CD, OUT_FLT_NO, OUT_FLT_SFX_CD,
OUT_DEP_FLTDT, OUT_DEP_FLTTM, OUT_ARR_FLTDT, OUT_PAX_TML_CD,
OUT_GROUND_ACY_CD, OUT_SERVICE_TYP, OUT_FLT_LEG_SEQ_NO, AIRCRAFT_OWNER_CD,
CARRIER_AC_TYP, MIDNIGHT_QTY, BUFFER_DUR, STD_WORKING_DUR, TOW_TIME_DUR,
FIXED_LINK_RSN_TXT, LINK_EFFECTIVE_DT, LINK_EXPIRY_DT, CURRENT_REC_IND )`.

### SELECT projection (33 expressions)

Each expression is a `NEW_*` column from `STAGING.ExpFinalyseInserts S`,
positionally aligned to the target. Several carry `_SMALLINT` or `_DATE`
suffixes (e.g. `NEW_IN_FLT_NO_SMALLINT`, `NEW_IN_DEP_FLTDT_DATE`) indicating
they were pre-cast in the upstream staging view. These suffixes describe the
*staging* cast, not the *target* column type — a SEM-06 type-compatibility
risk.

### Outer WHERE

`WHERE S.IN_FLT_LEG_SEQ_NO IS NOT NULL AND S.OUT_FLT_LEG_SEQ_NO IS NOT NULL`
— only inserts links where both the inbound and outbound leg sequence numbers
were successfully resolved (i.e. the legs exist in the schedule). The other 31
keys are not NULL-guarded here; their NULL handling is delegated to the
`NOT EXISTS` anti-join.

### NOT EXISTS anti-join (33-key)

`NOT EXISTS ( SELECT 1 FROM BASE.FLT_FOLDER_LINKS T WHERE T.<col> =
S.NEW_<col> AND … )` for all 33 columns. A staging row is inserted only when
no existing target row matches on *all 33* columns. This is the explicit
dedup: if a matching row already exists, the insert is suppressed. This
mirrors Teradata SET-table semantics (full-row duplicate drop) implemented at
the application level, since Snowflake has no SET table type.

### What the buggy input would have done instead

The buggy input was mechanically clean and functionally identical — no SQL
logic was changed. The entire remediation is `TODO(SME)` markers at the two
semantic-risk sites (the `NOT EXISTS` predicate block for SEM-03, and the
`_SMALLINT`/`_DATE` alias positions for SEM-06).

---

