## 6. Inline anchors

```anchors
UPDATE BASE.FLT_FOLDERLINKS tgt :: Update target: expire/update link records in the base table
SET
    LINK_EXPIRY_DT  = src.LINK_EXPIRY_DT,
    CURRENT_REC_IND = src.CURRENT_REC_IND :: SET clause: update expiry date and current-record indicator from the staging source
OLD_IN_DEP_FLIGHT_DT AS IN_DEP_FLIGHT_DT, -- TODO(SME): DEF-07 alias repaired :: DEF-07: alias renamed from IN_DEP_GMTFLIGHT_FLIGHT_DT to IN_DEP_FLIGHT_DT to match outer references
IFF(
            TO_CHAR(OLD_LINK_EXPIRY_DT,'YYYYMMDD') <> '20501231',
            OLD_LINK_EXPIRY_DT,
            DATEADD(DAY,-1,TO_DATE('<% ctx.env.S_vw6122_CompareLinksRecordsWithTeradata_Current_date %>','DDMONYY')) :: Expiry logic: if old expiry is the 20501231 sentinel, expire at Current_date-1; else keep old expiry (SEM-06/08 NULL fallthrough)
IFF(ACTION_CODE = 'U','Y','N') AS CURRENT_REC_IND :: Current-record indicator: Y for pure updates, N for both (insert+update)
WHERE ACTION_CODE IN ('U','B') :: Source filter: only update and both change records drive the expiry
WHERE tgt.LINK_STATION_CD       = src.LINK_STATION_CD :: 8-key join: match target rows to staging source on link identity
AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM BASE.FLIGHT_FOLDERLINKS x :: DEF-07: guard table name differs from UPDATE target (FLT_FOLDERLINKS vs FLIGHT_FOLDERLINKS) — SME
          AND x.LINK_EXPIRY_DT    = src.LINK_EXPIRY_DT
          AND x.CURRENT_REC_IND   = src.CURRENT_REC_IND :: Anti-join: suppress update if a row already exists with the new expiry/indicator (prevent re-processing)
```

